# Files GitHub Pages publishes. Nothing else in this repo is served.
# One path per line, relative to the repo root. A line containing *, ? or [
# is a glob that stays inside its folder (it never crosses a /) and must
# match at least one file. A missing path, an empty glob, or a path outside the repo fails the
# deploy, and the live site stays as it was. Add a line only for a file the
# page itself loads; never notes, tools, protocols or config.
# !path = known, deliberately not published. @prefix/ = watched area: every
# tracked file under it must match a line, or the run fails. A * never
# matches a leading dot: list dotfiles explicitly. Symlinks are refused.
# Only simple [ ] sets ([abc], [!x], [^x]) are allowed, and no wildcard on an @
# line; pages.yml's header lists everything that stops a deploy.
index.html
robots.txt
data/index.json
data/history.json
data/panels/*.json
!data/.last-check
@data/
